Rainbow six siege has breached its way  into closed alpha so it's time to talk  strategy there are 10 operators  available five attackers and five  defenders each with their own unique  ability knowing how your skills fit into  the team dynamic is going to give you an  edge so you can pull off some sweet  coordinated maneuvers instead like just  dying a whole lot let's start with the  attacking team and the dude you'll  probably pick first sledge who doesn't  want to be a badass with a hammer they  can just bash through stuff willy-nilly  but you never want to be the only one  breaching it's too obvious coordinate  with a teammate or set up your own  breach charge and then swing your hammer  while your enemies are looking at the  explosions and if your teammates have  the enemy distracted sledge can make  some great flanking runs and pop up  where he's least expected twitch is the  opposite of sledge not meant to lead the  charge or flank but rather to support a  team push she has a deployable drone  that's similar to what you use in the  scouting phase ideally your whole team  has parked their Scout drones in good  out-of-the-way places allowing you to  check their camera feed for Intel but if  not twitch has your mid-match scouting  covered her drone can also shock enemies  for 15 points of damage making it good  for downing enemies that are already  damaged by grenades gas or gunfire it  can also disarm traps if you're sharp  enough to spot them or if your enemy is  dull enough to put them out in the open  thermite's up next and what the thermite  do thermite's things it's right there in  the name thermite will blow a hole in  any reinforced wall no problem but it  sure takes its sweet-ass time  enemies can see and hear the fuse  burning so thermite makes a great  distraction while you execute another  breach or flanking move at the very  least avoid rushing in right after your  thermite blows unless you've chucked in  some grenades or are following the  recruit with the riot shield the recruit  is like the sixth man whose unique  ability is the riot shield but the  shield actually replaces his primary  weapon it's good for going through  breach holes provided you're crouching  to protect your legs and for peppering  pistol shots through barricades and  walls enemies firing back at you through  the wall will probably hit the shield  suckers Thatcher is another attacker and  his specialty is meddling with  electronics given that the defenders  have the most annoying and possibly  overpowered piece of kit in the game the  heartbeat sensor Thatcher's EMP grenades  can really help cover your advance while  your team is moving into breech position  and if one of your breach charge fails  to detonate there's probably a jammer  nearby just waiting to be fried by  Thatcher's grenade don't leave any EMP  grenades in your pockets you never know  when a c4 charge or gas trap is going to  be waiting right around the corner the  last attacker is Ashe she rocks the  breach charge launcher which basically  fires barricade busting grenades and is  super badass she can breach with the  speed of sledgehammer but with the  safety of projectile distance so you  sort of confuse the enemy with  simultaneous breaches support a push  with a quick follow-up reach or just  mess with the defenders mines by  breaching surfaces you aren't actually  near and have no intention of going  through psychological warfare is a must  in siege psyching out defenders can  encourage them to make mistakes mistakes  that you can capitalize on so how do you  avoid making mistakes on defense  coordinate your barricade placement with  your team designate one player to shoot  drones during the scouting phase consult  your security cameras when the attackers  are on the move and don't just freak out  when all the breaches start coming  because they're gonna come you can help  delay the breaching and throttle the  scouting by using mute the defender with  the jammer place these juiced-up  wireless routers behind walls to block  remote breaches and run to a choke point  during the scouting phase to block the  drone parade the range is pretty short  on these guys though so place them  carefully and when the action shifts  from the place your jamming to the place  you're not jamming just pick that little  bad boy up and take it with you if mute  blocks gadgets smoke blocks people with  remote detonated gas bombs smoke can  turn a hallway into a death trap or at  least do some sweet area denial setting  these traps near entryways can stop the  enemy short burning precious seconds off  the clock and bringing your victory ever  closer toss one to where the enemy is  grouping up to scatter them or Chuck one  into a recently breached hole to make  them think twice about coming in slowing  the attackers advance is  great defensive tactic and the strong  barricades that castle can place do just  that  it takes an enemy three melee hits to  break down a normal barricade castles  barriers force the enemy to burn time  actually breaching and if mute puts a  jammer behind one then the breach charge  they spend all that time unfolding was  all for naught  castles barriers offer cover from enemy  fire as opposed to the mere concealment  offered by normal barricades cover  protects you from bullets concealment  does not learn the difference give  yourself a defensive edge by placing a  deployable shield down next to the wall  you want to shoot through and if you put  it near the door that's totally blocked  up castle has got that area locked down  if or rather when you happen to catch a  bullet or two you'll be glad to have  look on your team  rooks deployable bag of armor will  either fortify you from the start or  patch you up mid match a downed player  gets revived at half health but if  there's armor waiting you'll have a full  strength fighter back in no time  if you deploy the armor bag early then  rook is free to go off on flanking  maneuvers without depriving his allies  of the benefits of his unique skill just  remember that if you go outside have a  plan to get back inside quickly or  prepare to deal with the aggression  coming your way when the game  automatically points you out to your  enemies and finally the last defender is  the guy who looks like a jerk and uses  the jerkiest gadget around pulse his  heart rate monitor is awesome to use and  so aggravating to plan around so be sure  to stay alive and keep it in play as  long as possible  sniffing out enemies and calling out  their position is a great way to give  your team an advantage and if you find  the right angles to shoot them through  floors or ceilings well that's a great  move just be sure you know the map well  enough not to expose yourself while  you've got your eyes glued to the screen  play to the strengths of each character  and communicate with your teammates and  you'll be on your way to saving or  protecting an innocent life just kidding  no-one saves the hostage share your own  tips in the comments below and happy  hunting
 

